  ('1052183373738675604', 'El placer de matar', 1988, 'Action, Thriller', 'Félix Rotaeta', null, 'Antonio Banderas, Mathieu Carrière, Victoria Abril, Berta Riaza', null, 'Two assassins: Luis, young and impulsive and André, married teacher. Fate lets them cross their lines, evident in the same victim. From the beginning they like each other; and both become addicted to killing synchronously.', 'Two assassins: Luis, young and impulsive and André, married teacher. Fate lets them cross their lines, evident in the same victim. From the beginning they like each other; and both become addicted to killing synchronously.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/ymSEVFsghtriOt5vq6bKa5ZtHed.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:190070'),
  ('714903073961658815', 'El Planeta', 2021, 'Comedy, Drama', 'Amalia Ulman, Carlos Rigo, Carmen Roca Igual', 'Amalia Ulman', 'Ale Ulman, Amalia Ulman, Nacho Vigalondo, Genoveva Garcia Castanon, Saoirse Bertram, Andrea Escobar, Zhou Chen, Carlos Carbonell', 'NR', 'Amidst the devastation of post-crisis Spain, mother and daughter bluff and grift to keep up the lifestyle they think they deserve, bonding over common tragedy and an impending eviction.', 'Amidst the devastation of post-crisis Spain, mother and daughter bluff and grift to keep up the lifestyle they think they deserve, bonding over common tragedy and an impending eviction.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/fsjc9edVdY7kxuC3889h1XWxTsv.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:776536'),
  ('591854035481404394', 'El Polaquito', 2003, 'Drama, Action', 'Juan Carlos Desanzo, Carlos Torlaschi', 'Juan Carlos Desanzo, Lito Espinosa', 'Abel Ayala, Marina Glezer, Fernando Roa, Roly Serrano, Víctor Hugo Carrizo, Osvaldo Sanders, Fabián Arenillas', null, 'At age 13, a street kid known as "El Polaquito" makes his living mostly by singing tangos on Buenos Aires commuter trains. He falls in love with a 16 year old prostitute, also working for the Mafia controlling child exploitation in one of Argentina''s busiest train stations. He tries to rescue her from this cruel life with no future. But to do so, he must confront the ruthless adult gang leaders, as well as the young kids who protect them, believing that this Mafia is truly their only option.', 'At age 13, a street kid known as "El Polaquito" makes his living mostly by singing tangos on Buenos Aires commuter trains. He falls in love with a 16 year old prostitute, also working for the Mafia controlling child exploitation in one of Argentina''s busiest train stations. He tries to rescue her from this cruel life with no future. But to do so, he must confront the ruthless adult gang leaders, as well as the young kids who protect them, believing that this Mafia is truly their only option.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/oECJ0oMrB7JBNwzRmLiPGGtS3QC.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:92597'),
  ('519950672765037637', 'El Portero', 1950, 'Comedy', 'Miguel M. Delgado, Raúl Martínez Solares, Julio Cahero', 'Miguel M. Delgado, Jaime Salvador', 'Cantinflas, Silvia Pinal, Carlos Martínez Baena, Óscar Pulido, Fernando Casanova, José Baviera, Josefina del Mar, Conchita Gentil Arcos', null, 'Cantinflas works as a porter, who writes letters and speeches in his old writing machine to earn an extra money, despite the fact that he still goes to school. The sentimental issues come when Cantinflas falls in love of his pretty neighborhood (Silvia Pinal), who is handicapped and unable to walk. The thing wont be easy, because a young military man also has feelings for the girl. But the porter wants to see her happy, and he will become a sort of Cyrano De Bergerac, writing love letters to her signed by the young soldier. His plan is simple: to win money in the horse races in order to pay the operation which will make her walk again.', 'Cantinflas works as a porter, who writes letters and speeches in his old writing machine to earn an extra money, despite the fact that he still goes to school. The sentimental issues come when Cantinflas falls in love of his pretty neighborhood (Silvia Pinal), who is handicapped and unable to walk. The thing wont be easy, because a young military man also has feelings for the girl. But the porter wants to see her happy, and he will become a sort of Cyrano De Bergerac, writing love letters to her signed by the young soldier. His plan is simple: to win money in the horse races in order to pay the operation which will make her walk again.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/zjbE6ufnJqf6qvaiMvEavs77cSB.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:82778'),
  ('649675850219012586', 'El Potro: Unstoppable', 2018, 'Drama, Music', 'Daniel Ortega, Lucas Outeda, Luis Bernárdez', null, 'Rodrigo Romero, Florencia Peña, Jimena Barón, Fernán Mirás, Malena Sánchez, Daniel Aráoz, Diego Cremonesi, Adriana Balbo', null, 'A young man with charisma and magnetism enters the atmosphere of tropical music as a romantic singer and undertakes a vertiginous ascent to fame.', 'A young man with charisma and magnetism enters the atmosphere of tropical music as a romantic singer and undertakes a vertiginous ascent to fame.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/vjscS1uhpgcrJe3U72p4nBAWx3T.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:552180'),
  ('1047514403412388406', 'El pozolero', 2009, 'Crime', 'Alonso O. Lara', 'Alonso O. Lara', 'John Solis, Eleazar García Jr., Juan Garcia, Óscar López, Joel Navarro, Amador Granados, Benigno Tovar', null, 'Man with a talent for making the bodies disappear finds a niche in a drug cartel.', 'Man with a talent for making the bodies disappear finds a niche in a drug cartel.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/wyCXPu4Y2wI6jJi6FoGffgpCQ8R.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:373327'),
  ('1072277563996147438', 'El principio', 1973, 'Action, Drama, History', 'Gonzalo Martínez Ortega', 'Gonzalo Martínez Ortega', 'Lucha Villa, Narciso Busquets, Andrés García, Fernando Balzaretti, Sergio Bustamante, Aurora Clavel, Patricia Aspíllaga, Evangelina Martínez', null, 'Mexico is in the midst of Revolution when the protagonist returns after studying in Paris to find his native town in Chihuahua occupied by Francisco Villa’s revolutionary forces. He visits his deserted home and remembers people and events from his adolescence that provide glimpses of pre-Revolutionary society under dictatorship: his uncle, the chief of police; his sister’s involvement with a liberal political association; bathing with the girls from a local brothel; a labor strike that ended in a massacre. Returning to the present he discovers that his father has been assassinated and, in the company of his father’s former servant, joins the revolutionary movement.', 'Mexico is in the midst of Revolution when the protagonist returns after studying in Paris to find his native town in Chihuahua occupied by Francisco Villa’s revolutionary forces. He visits his deserted home and remembers people and events from his adolescence that provide glimpses of pre-Revolutionary society under dictatorship: his uncle, the chief of police; his sister’s involvement with a liberal political association; bathing with the girls from a local brothel; a labor strike that ended in a massacre. Returning to the present he discovers that his father has been assassinated and, in the company of his father’s former servant, joins the revolutionary movement.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/vKvlQdxzmdzEW0NYinyP1sd2j1.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:78100'),
