  ('596627984480100276', 'Eugene, Little Eugene and Katyusha', 1967, 'Comedy, Romance, War, Drama', 'Vladimir Motyl, Konstantin Ryzhov, Yevgeni Nesterov', 'Bulat Okudzhava, Vladimir Motyl', 'Oleg Dal, Galina Figlovskaya, Georgiy Shtil, Pavel Morozenko, Mikhail Kokshenov, Mark Bernes, Vladimir Ilin, Nikolai Godovikov', null, 'War, 1944. Soldier Zhenya Kolyshkin, a fragile intellectual from Arbat, sets out on New Year''s Eve to collect a parcel, but stumbles upon a German dugout. He manages to escape, but guard duty is inevitable. Zhenya''s predicament is brightened by Zhenechka, a communications officer in the Katyusha regiment.', 'War, 1944. Soldier Zhenya Kolyshkin, a fragile intellectual from Arbat, sets out on New Year''s Eve to collect a parcel, but stumbles upon a German dugout. He manages to escape, but guard duty is inevitable. Zhenya''s predicament is brightened by Zhenechka, a communications officer in the Katyusha regiment.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/aJpofFPvw7fxp6axijwyUANCBbo.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:89675'),
